ood Walk of Fame for his achievements in music. He was inducted into the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame in 2013 as the winner, alongside Quincy Jones, of the Ahmet Ertegun Award.\n\n", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2023-08-01T15:58:59.264515+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 2595, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lou_Adler"}], "uuid": "3b256d39-4369-4de2-bb97-57dab5aab325", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "24004", "external_references": [{"id": 11079, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q568770"}, {"id": 11080, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "10054240"}, {"id": 11081, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "no99079564"}, {"id": 11082, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-no99079564"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-05T22:30:29.988503+10:00"}, {"id": 76464, "name": "Christopher Renshaw", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 898970, "title": "The Mikado", "work_id": 79458, "role": "co-director", "role_id": 959, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": null, "date_of_death": null, "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": null, "external_links": [], "uuid": "3dcd23a5-8dfd-4d13-a547-5e420834b95f", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": null, "external_references": [{"id": 43039, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q121299534"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-05T18:36:43.766025+10:00"}, {"id": 76463, "name": "R.A. Weinberg", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2191068, "title": "Pavlova", "work_id": 79456, "role": "co-producer", "role_id": 915, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "", "biography_author": null, "dat